1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,569
An agent just opened a pull request. Do
you ship it today?

2
00:00:06,169 --> 00:00:10,251
Most teams rubber stamp the diff, or
rewrite the whole thing.

3
00:00:11,801 --> 00:00:14,226
Read the diff, not the summary.

4
00:00:15,196 --> 00:00:16,770
Run it once yourself.

5
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,557
Ask what it does not handle.

6
00:00:21,107 --> 00:00:24,318
Sixty seconds of reading is the whole
budget.

7
00:00:25,868 --> 00:00:27,916
Forty seconds reading the diff.

8
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:31,004
Ten seconds running it yourself.

9
00:00:31,974 --> 00:00:35,719
Ten seconds asking what it quietly refuses
to handle.

10
00:00:37,269 --> 00:00:41,032
One command runs every check: npm test.

11
00:00:42,582 --> 00:00:46,019
Green means merge. Red means send it back.

12
00:00:47,569 --> 00:00:52,018
Three checks. One command. A minute of
your time.

13
00:00:53,568 --> 00:00:58,985
Pick one repository this week. Run the
checks. That is the method.
